    {
      "id": "PKri",
      "code_hash": "3187680a53a39b9c3135d5cd92c03f59",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert\"><h2 id=\"coding-nomenclature\">Coding Nomenclature</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The text uses the notation <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(x_{ij}||)</marimo-tex> to denote the value at the index <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(i,j||)</marimo-tex> in the matrix <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(x \\in \\mathbb{R}^{N \\times N}||)</marimo-tex> and the notation <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(x_i||)</marimo-tex> to denote the value at the index <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(i||)</marimo-tex> in the vector <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(x \n\\in \\mathbb{R}^N||)</marimo-tex>.  To disambiguate cases where the variable <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(x||)</marimo-tex> denotes two different things depending on the dimensions of the variable, the code in this notebook will always use capitalized variables for 2-dimensional arrays and lowercase variable names to 1-dimensional arrays.  Thus <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(x_i||)</marimo-tex> will always be coded as <code>x[i]</code>, while <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(x_{i,j}||)</marimo-tex> will be coded as <code>X[i,j]</code>. Scalars will be coded as <code>x_&lt;tag&gt;</code> to indicate that they are not arrays. In cases where variables are denoted <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(x^Y_{i}||)</marimo-tex> or <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(x^Y_{i,j}||)</marimo-tex>, these will be coded as <code>xY[i]</code> and <code>XY[i,j]</code>, respectively. </span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Additional variable encodings include the following:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\underline x, \\bar x, \\hat x, \\v x, \\tilde x, \\dot x, \\ddot x \\cdots \\to||)</marimo-tex> <code>xmin</code>, <code>xmax</code>, <code>xhat</code>, <code>xvee</code>, <code>xtilde</code>, <code>xdot</code>,<code>xddot</code>, ...</li>\n<li><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma,\\cdots \\to||)</marimo-tex> <code>alpha</code>, <code>beta</code>, <code>gamma</code>, ...</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
