    {
      "id": "RGSE",
      "code_hash": "1f1a3ca38dde14925300bee25def6511",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert\"><span class=\"paragraph\">The real power flow <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(p_{ij}||)</marimo-tex> and reactive power flow <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(q_{ij}||)</marimo-tex> on the power lines from the nodes <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(i||)</marimo-tex> to the nodes <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(j||)</marimo-tex> must remain below the lines' capacities such that <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(p_{ij}^2+q_{ij}^2 \n\\le \\bar s_{ij}^2||)</marimo-tex>. Note that in the <code>pypower</code> cases, the line limit is nominally <code>rateA</code>, with <code>rateB</code> and <code>rateC</code> reserved for emergency line ratings only.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
